  slide "A · Process boundary" {
    eyebrow: "PROCESS BOUNDARY · PROTOCOL V2"
    title: "The stdio entry point and the wire contract"
    lede: "stdout is the protocol channel; everything else is stderr."
    narration: "Component A — the process boundary. A green letter badge 'A' with the kicker 'process boundary · protocol v2'. stdin carries the envelope into aiperf-runner; stdout is the protocol channel; stderr is tracing. Argument dispatch: --capabilities emits the plugins catalog, --cell runs one cell, cells>1 is the cellular controller, and the default is a single-process execute. The wire contract: RunnerEnvelopeV2 is strict deny_unknown_fields while the embedded config stays open, and into_authored() decides scheduled vs graph from the dataset format, yielding AuthoredRunSpecV2."
    caption: "stdio boundary · strict envelope · argument dispatch."
    render: @scene {
      sdk.Shape(id = "pb-badge", variant = "rect", label = "A", x = 40, y = 16, width = 34, height = 34, surfaceRole = theme(accent.primary))
      sdk.Label(id = "pb-badge-l", text = "A", x = 40, y = 23, width = 34, height = 20, inkRole = theme(ink.primary))
      sdk.Caption(id = "pb-kicker", text = "PROCESS BOUNDARY · PROTOCOL V2", x = 84, y = 24, width = 500, height = 18, inkRole = theme(accent.primary))
